sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," In his first charge, the psalmist blames the Lord for his demise. God’s overpowering anger did not make sense. • The phrase ",{"c":["the darkest depths"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," implies the place of the dead (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.143.3","r":"Ps.143.3","rawR":"Ps.143.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.143.3","value":"Ps.143.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"143:3"},"; see ",{"href":"?bref=Lam.3.6","r":"Lam.3.6","rawR":"Lam.3.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lam.3.6","value":"Lam.3.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lam 3:6"},") or the depths of the sea (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.68.22","r":"Ps.68.22","rawR":"Ps.68.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.68.22","value":"Ps.68.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 68:22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.69.1-2","r":"Ps.69.1-2","rawR":"Ps.69.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.69.1-2","value":"Ps.69.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"69:1-2"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.88.6-7","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":88,"endVerse":7,"startChapter":88,"startVerse":6}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.88.6-7","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[88],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"ad75c01b49f1ea806f585abafa22a285ffbec3a67ceec365e206d670dcaa0dc3","sourceItemName":"Ps.88.6-7","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6884,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.88.6-7","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.88.6-7","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.88.8-12","r":"Ps.88.8-12","rawR":"Ps.88.8-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.88.8-12","value":"Ps.88.8-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"88:8-12"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," In his second charge, the psalmist claims that God has isolated him and caused his loneliness (cp. ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.31.11","r":"Ps.31.11","rawR":"Ps.31.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.31.11","value":"Ps.31.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"31:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.38.11","r":"Ps.38.11","rawR":"Ps.38.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.38.11","value":"Ps.38.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"38:11"},"). Loneliness was a curse in a culture where relationships were more important than personal achievement."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.88.8-12","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":88,"endVerse":12,"startChapter":88,"startVerse":8}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.88.8-12","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[88],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"9ba08baf2b2e28ae1266849b80a2cd7a6c4ceaf976530d64eba49b497aef4833","sourceItemName":"Ps.88.8-12","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6885,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.88.8-12","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.88.8-12","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.88.13-17","r":"Ps.88.13-17","rawR":"Ps.88.13-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.88.13-17","value":"Ps.88.13-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"88:13-17"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," In his third charge, the psalmist accuses the Lord of rejecting him. The force and apparent cruelty of the psalmist’s suffering overwhelm him."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.88.13-17","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":88,"endVerse":17,"startChapter":88,"startVerse":13}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.88.13-17","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":